- Repaired the backend compile blocker in `refund-manual.ts` by removing the stray buyer-consumible execute branch from `approveRefundManualCase()` and keeping buyer consumibles on explicit execute/reject resolution paths only.
- Added a shared buyer consumibles contract for `mis-compras` and `mis-tickets`, including `venta_item_id`, refund metadata, and `resuelto_parcial` typing.
- Added runtime proof in `backend/src/consumibles-buyer-partial-refunds.test.ts` that both `rejected` and `resolved_non_refundable` outcomes keep the originally requested quantity redeemable.
- Added explicit pending-review proof in backend and buyer UI tests so a `requested` consumible refund still renders as manual review and does not reduce redeemable quantity before execution.
- Added buyer-visible copy coverage for `rejected` and `resolved_non_refundable` consumible outcomes so final non-executed resolutions are explicit instead of being hidden behind generic availability text.
- Re-verified: `backend` typecheck passes, `src/consumibles-buyer-partial-refunds.test.ts` passes, and targeted frontend type errors for buyer consumibles no longer appear in `platea` typecheck output.

